<title>COSTA RICA: SOCCER-COSTA RICA THROUGH TO CONCACAF SEMIFINALS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-COSTA RICA THROUGH TO CONCACAF SEMIFINALS.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Costa Rica 1996-12-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Costa Rica beat Trinidad and Tabago 2-1 (halftime 1-1) in their CONCACAF semifinal stage group one World Cup qualifier Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Costa Rica - Paulo Cesar Wanchope (9,10)</p>
<p>Trinidad and Tobago - Jerren Nixon (11th)</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p>(tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>    United States	6  4  1  1 10  5 13</p>
<p>    Costa Rica	   6  4  0  2  9  5 12</p>
<p>    Guatemala	    6  2  2  2  6  9  8</p>
<p>    Trinidad	     6  0  1  5  3  9  1</p>
<p>Note - top two qualify for the six-team final stage of the CONCACAF World Cup qualifiers.</p>
</text>
